ity regarding yogita's situation.", "yogita's health & availability for stand-up: yogita states she is not feeling well. yogita is unsure if she can attend the morning stand-up. yogita anticipates being able to connect with rohan in the afternoon. she expresses her best effort to connect. this highlights potential disruptions to the daily workflow. rohan acknowledges yogita's situation.", "organic social media performance & boosting strategy: discussion of low follower growth despite consistent posting since october 2nd. rohan explained the need to boost existing posts to increase visibility. yogita's team will determine which posts to boost and provide a rationale. the boosting strategy aims to overcome organic reach limitations. the team is analyzing the performance of existing content. rohan confirmed a budget has been allocated for february boosting. the goal is to drive follower growth and engagement. the team will monitor the results of the boosting campaign. discussion of the importance of content quality and relevance.", "workflow and logistics - stand-up meetings & access to resources: dhruvik mentioned having a stand-up meeting. rohan inquired about harsh's access to dockmost spaces. harsh confirmed he had started going through the resources in dockmost. there was a brief discussion about the amount of data in dockmost.", "lifestyle & stylized images: discussion about the availability of lifestyle and stylized editorial images. dhruvik mentions that lifestyle images are already available for some categories. confirmation that the team has access to these images. brief mention of the use of these images in the overall visual strategy.", "content calendar & visual asset creation: rohan asks dhruvik to share the document with cropping details. dhruvik confirms he will share the document. discussion of creating a template for generating visual assets. dhruvik mentions he'll try creating the template and share it with rohan. rohan has created a separate chat for testing and receiving suggestions. dhruvik will use this chat for feedback and iteration. discussion of the overall workflow for creating visual assets and ensuring quality.", "story vs. feed content & aesthetic considerations: gayatri suggests that some of the ideas discussed are better suited for instagram stories rather than feed posts. discussion of the aesthetic appeal of the visuals and the need for a visually appealing representation of the product. the team is looking for a way to create visually appealing content that is both informative and engaging. discussion of the challenges of creating visually appealing content that is also informative. gayatri suggests that the team should focus on creating visually appealing content that is also informative and engaging. viraj suggests focusing on ingredient visualization as a way to overcome the challenges of creating visually appealing content. discussion about the potential of using instagram stories to showcase visually appealing content that is also informative.", "historical context - prior decisions: rohan kumar will procure a small monitor (2-3k) for his setup. rohan will send harsh the link to the design stand-up meeting (shared on mattermost). rohan kumar will connect at 6:00 pm for an introduction of 'hush' to the team before leaving. rohan will share previous dashboard templates for harshh to review and use as a starting point for creating e-commerce dashboard templates. rohan will connect with chayan and dhruvik separately to discuss further. rohan will provide a dashboard template for tracking boosting metrics (followers, likes, etc.). rohan will discuss boosting a post with yogita in the morning. this segment summarized previously agreed-upon actions and decisions.", "initial website link sharing & task overview: rohan kumar was not at pf.growthsupercharge.com. rohan kumar forgot to share the website link. rohan kumar intended to share the link immediately. harsh sharma clarified the website represented the core team's work. harsh sharma explained the website contained a task column. harsh sharma stated the team was gradually building functionality. harsh sharma anticipated the functionality would be fully fleshed out in the next couple of weeks. harsh sharma thanked rohan. the discussion focused on providing access to the team's ongoing work and outlining progress.", "communication channels & support - town square, town club, mattermost: harsh sharma is encouraged to use the town square or town club for asking questions. mattermost is used for sharing links and information. rohan kumar shared the design stand-up link on mattermost. the team is emphasizing the importance of clear communication and collaboration. discussion about the availability of support and resources for new team members. the team is encouraging harsh sharma to actively participate in communication channels. the team is aiming to create a supportive and collaborative environment. the team is emphasizing the importance of seeking help when needed.", "scheduling & availability - yogita & sameera: sameera mentions her 'start stand-up' doesn't happen in the evening. she plans to connect with yogita separately because she won't be at home in the evening. this indicates a need to coordinate schedules and find a time that works for both sameera and yogita. there's an implicit acknowledgment of the challenges of coordinating schedules with remote or busy team members. this is a logistical concern that needs to be addressed to ensure effective communication and collaboration. the team is aiming for a collaborative approach to content creation. emphasis on sharing ideas and building upon each other's work. the team is trying to distribute tasks based on individual skills and interests. the team is encouraging each member to take ownership of specific content areas.", "ugc (user generated content) & kaitri: rohan will focus on influencer outreach, yogita will handle ugc later. discussion about kaitri