e a detailed documentation.\\n  • Emphasis on the importance of capturing various error types for model training.\\n\\n[16:16 - 17:33] 📌 Training Data for AI Debugging Agent\\n  👥 Key participants: Isha Joshi, Rohan Kumar, Chayan Roy\\n  • Significant discussion around the challenges of generating a training dataset for the AI debugging agent.\\n  • The dataset needs to accurately capture various error types, warnings, and common logs.\\n  • Differentiating between these categories is crucial for model performance.\\n  • Isha emphasized the importance of a high-quality dataset for training an effective model.\\n  • Discussion on the use of coding LLMs for debugging.\\n  • The need to capture all types of errors to train the model effectively.\\n  • Importance of capturing the nuances between errors, warnings, and normal logs.\\n\\n[17:34 - 19:13] 📌 Harsh's Work & Dashboard Templates\\n  👥 Key participants: Rohan Kumar, Isha Joshi, Harsh (mentioned)\\n  • Rohan mentioned Harsh requested documentation and is working on dashboard templates.\\n  • Harsh will use Isha's previous work as a foundation for the templates.\\n  • The goal is to create templates that can be used with Google Sheets or Airbyte.\\n  • Isha will ensure all business definitions and formulas are included in the templates.\\n  • Rohan emphasized the importance of clear definitions for accurate data representation.\\n  • The team will collaborate to improve the dashboard templates based on feedback.\\n\\n[19:13 - 21:16] 📌 NATN and Existing Debugging Processes\\n  👥 Key participants: Rohan Kumar, Isha Joshi, Chayan Roy\\n  • Rohan mentioned a similar process exists in NATN that can connect to servers, check logs, and suggest basic fixes.\\n  • Isha's project aims to build upon this existing process with more detailed log checking and analysis.\\n  • The combination of NATN's process and Isha's detailed analysis could create a powerful debugging tool.\\n  • Discussion about the potential benefits of combining existing tools with new AI-powered features.\\n\\n[21:18 - 22:37] 📌 Exploration vs. Standard Reports in GA4\\n  👥 Key participants: Ayush Anand, Rohan Kumar\\n  • Discussion of the limitations of standard reports in GA4, focusing on their inability to handle non-linear user paths and loops.\\n  • Standard reports answer 'what happened' while explorations answer 'why did this happen, for whom?'\\n  • Standard reports collapse behavior into averages, hiding crucial details about user journeys.\\n  • Explorations allow for deeper analysis of user behavior, identifying pain points, successful paths, and areas for improvement.\\n  • Ayush Anand presented a document outlining the benefits of explorations and how they address the shortcomings of standard reports.\\n  • Emphasis on the need to understand user paths beyond linear funnels.\\n  • Discussion of how explorations reveal loops, dead ends, and unexpected success paths.\\n  • Rohan Kumar highlighted the importance of practice and hands-on experience to truly grasp the power of explorations.\\n  • Ayush Anand described a planned approach to documenting explorations for future reference and deeper questioning.\\n  • Explorations focus on understanding individual user journeys, while standard reports provide aggregated data.\\n  • The team agreed that explorations are crucial for uncovering insights that standard reports miss.\\n  • Explorations allow for the analysis of specific user segments and their unique behaviors.\\n  • Discussion of the benefits of using explorations to identify opportunities for optimization and personalization.\\n\\n[22:37 - 24:40] 📌 GA4 Exploration Document Review & Practical Application\\n  👥 Key participants: Ayush Anand, Rohan Kumar\\n  • Ayush Anand presented a document detailing the benefits of using explorations in GA4.\\n  • Rohan Kumar praised the document's clarity and succinctness.\\n  • Discussion about the need for hands-on practice to fully understand and apply explorations.\\n  • Rohan Kumar emphasized that understanding explorations requires more than just theoretical knowledge.\\n  • Ayush Anand described a planned approach to documenting explorations for뜹 future reference and deeper questioning.\\n  • The team agreed that explorations are crucial for uncovering insights that standard reports miss.\\n  • Rohan Kumar expressed a desire to see examples of how explorations can be used to solve specific business problems.\\n  • Discussion of the importance of being able to drill down into data and uncover hidden patterns.\\n  • Ayush Anand committed to sharing examples of explorations and demonstrating their practical application.\\n  • The team acknowledged that mastering explorations will require ongoing learning and experimentation.\\n  • Rohan Kumar highlighted the value of documenting explorations to share knowledge and best practices.\\n\\n[24:48 - 26:55] 📌 Network Connectivity and Failover Strategy\\n  👥 Key participants: Chayan Roy, Rohan Kumar\\n  • Discussion of network connectivity options and a strategy for ensuring service availability during outages.\\n  • The team discussed using multiple network connections (BSNL and another provider) for redundancy.\\n  • They explored the possibility of using a static IP address for failover.\\n  • The team acknowledged the limitations of using a single DNS record with multiple addresses.\\n  • Chayan Roy suggested creating a backup URL for the service during outages.\\n  • The team considered the possibility of using a service like Cloudflare tunnel for failover.\\n  • Discussion of the importance of seamless failover to minimize disruption to users.\\n  • The team agreed that it's crucial to be able to determine whether a service outage is due to a network issue or a server problem.\\n  • The team discussed the need for monitoring and alerting to detect network outages promptly.\\n  • Chayan Roy suggested that the service should remain accessible even if one network connection is d