 the follow-up was to solidify understanding and address any lingering issues.", "िकांत: rohan explains the three active verticals within pf: the g2c brand, the g2c consultancy, and the growth supercharge office os. discussion of the fundraising efforts for the office os, including exploring incubators, government grants, and pitch deck creation. explanation of how funding for the office os will impact team compensation. rohan highlights the potential for the office os to generate revenue and become a standalone business. discussion of the benefits of building internal tools and infrastructure for both pf and potential external clients. rohan emphasizes the importance of solving internal problems to create valuable solutions for others.", "team resource allocation & hiring: rohan inquired about dhruvik's need for a full-time or junior team member. rohan offered a budget of around 30k for a potential hire. rohan mentioned the possibility of continuing to onboard interns. rohan emphasized the importance of dhruvik's team in driving the e-commerce brand's strategy and output. dhruvik expressed a willingness to manage the workload but acknowledged the potential benefits of additional support. dhruvik suggested actively looking for interns. dhruvik proposed that if interns are insufficient, they would explore hiring a junior team member through their network. dhruvik mentioned they would consider interviewing and onboarding a junior team member if needed. discussion about balancing workload and maintaining quality output. rohan reiterated his willingness to provide resources if needed. dhruvik expressed gratitude for rohan's support. rohan highlighted the importance of avoiding excessive pressure on the team.", "follow-up discussion & time availability: rohan kumar requested time for a follow-up discussion. he inquired about chayan roy's availability. rohan kumar indicated a desire to discuss further details. the request suggests a need for more in-depth conversation. the discussion highlights the importance of ongoing communication. rohan kumar is seeking to ensure alignment and address any remaining questions. the team is committed to maintaining open lines of communication. the follow-up discussion is intended to facilitate collaboration and problem-solving.", "brand understanding & christian forest aesthetic: dhruvik inquired about sahil's familiarity with christian forest (the brand). dhruvik emphasized the importance of understanding the brand's aesthetic and design principles. dhruvik encouraged sahil to review christian forest's instagram handle to gain insights. discussion of the difference between working for a client versus a brand. dhruvik highlighted the importance of understanding the brand's visual language and applying it consistently. dhruvik explained the diverse range of content on christian forest’s instagram (static posts, reels, animations). dhruvik stressed the importance of understanding the brand's overall aesthetic and applying it to all design work. discussion of the use of ai in creating some of christian forest's content. dhruvik emphasized the need to channelize and utilize existing skills effectively when working with a brand. dhruvik reiterated the importance of reviewing christian forest’s instagram to understand their design aesthetic.", "cohort guesstimation - initial challenges: seema samanta struggled to find reliable percentages for aspirational premium investors and value maximization seekers. difficulty in accurately estimating the size of these segments within the premium market. concerns about the lack of data for conscious lifestyle adopters, who are sustainability-driven. discussion ofถุน potential missing filters in the initial guesstimation model. identification of the 8% income segment (earning over 10 lakhs) as a key area for refinement. rohan pointed out a potential error in the guesstimation logic related to the income segment. rohit was present in a previous discussion about the guesstimation process.", "e-commerce dashboard development & data analytics: rohan tasks the new hire with developing e-commerce dashboard templates. the dashboards should include l1, l2, and l3 kpis (revenue, spend, ctr, etc.). rohan will share previous dashboard examples for reference. discussion of the importance of tracking key metrics and understanding data-driven insights. rohan mentions existing work with isha and ayush, interns focused on data analytics. ayush is currently focused on ga4 and performance marketing. the new hire will be responsible for assisting ayush with харьків doubts and issues.", "incubator & grant research - data scraping & column headers: seema shares that aryan has scraped data for incubator research. aryan is adding data to remaining columns. discussion of criteria for evaluating incubators. seema explains her approach to defining evaluation criteria. rohan approves the column headers and confirms alignment with brand values. seema outlines the process of using the data to identify suitable incubators. the goal is to identify incubators that align with the startup's needs and stage. rohan requests seema to provide context to harsh regarding the incubator research. seema explains the connection between grants, incubators, and funding opportunities. discussion of the sisf seed fund startup india scheme. emphasis on identifying incubators that can help secure funding. rohan reiterates the importance of aligning the research with brand values and target audience.", "market segmentation and cohort definition: discussion centers on defining customer segments for targeting, specifically focusing on income levels and purchasing power. initial discussion on the percentage of women in billionaire/millionaire categories (12-18%, aiming for 20-25% for realistic representation). debate on whether to increase the 8% representation of aspirational premium buyers due to new data. clarification that the 8% previously represented income above 10 lakhs, while the 3% represents above 20 lakhs. seema suggests needing to define the percentage of people with income between 5-15 lakhs to accurately represent the aspirational premium segment. reference to a survey indicating 80% of the population has a pci (per capita income) around 1.2-1.3 lakhs. discussion of the validity of the 80% pci figure, acknowledging the vast income disparity in india. emphasis on the importance of disposable income as a better indicator of purchasing power. debate on whether to adjust the percentages based on new data and ensure mutually exclusive cohorts. seema wants to define the percentage of people earning between 5-15 lakhs. reference to a survey showing 7-8% of the population has income above 10 lakhs and 70-72% below 5 lakhs. regering to the article stating that only the top 10% of the population falls in the income bracket wherein their net worth is more than 25 lakh rupees. discussion about the difference between net worth and disposable income. harsh offered to share census data on income. rohan emphasizes the importance of defining a smaller, well-defined cohort for targeted marketing. seema wants to determine the percentage of people with income above 15 lakhs. discussion about the importance of defining mutually exclusive cohorts for accurate targeting.", "growth stand-up meetings & research depth: rohan explains that the growth stand-up meetings tend to be longer. he focuses on creating a deeper understanding of the research topics. rohan wants to ensure that team members can connect the dots and understand the context of their work. he believes that a more thorough explanation upfront saves time in the long run. rohan wants the team to understand the 'why' behind the research. he emphasizes the importance of connecting research to practical applications. the goal is to create a more informed and effective research process.", "gayatri's daily plan: gayatri outlined her plan to create more videos and address other content-related tasks. confirmation of gayatri's plan to focus on video creation and content review.", "candidate shortlisting process improvement: rohan highlights the importance of maximizing output from shortlisted candidates. discussion on the two-step process: shortlisting and conversation. identification of a significant drop-off rate during the conversation stage. need to ensure the drop-off is not due to insufficient effort. rohan emphasizes the importance of thoroughly reviewing the 20 shortlisted resumes. chayan roy will increase the daily interview threshold to improve output.", "boost campaign & payment: request to approve a boost campaign payment of 10,000 rupees. yogita will share a qr code for payment. discussion of the launch date (around february 26th or 27th). rohan is unavailable from february 22nd onwards. goal is to complete the launch design before february 21st. yogita confirms rohan's unavailability from february 22nd to the end of february. discussion of a tentative launch date around february 26th or 27th.", "initial project discussion & budget confirmation: gayatri and sidra are discussing starting a project immediately. the project's feasibility is contingent on budget availability. if the project exceeds the current budget, it will be postponed to the next or following month. sidra confirms she is 'on it' and will send an email detailing the discussed points. sidra will allow gayatri to choose key concept products to begin with. gayatri requests sidra's email address. sidra confirms she will send her email address via whatsapp chat. both express hope for a long-term working relationship. they conclude the conversation with well wishes and a 'bye-bye'.", "ad campaign status & publication: gayatri confirms she is publishing content 'right now'. confirmation that funds have been added for the ad campaign. gayatri is publishing the content. discussion of which posts are currently running ads – specifically, only the first post is confirmed. gayatri and yogita confirm the ad is running on the first post. acknowledgement and thanks between gayatri and yogita. brief exchange confirming ad status and completion of publishing.", "job posting & linkedin ad campaign: discussion of posting a job ad on linkedin for interns. need to connect with chayan regarding a google form for the application process. rohan will provide assistance with creating the google form. details about adding a budget of 500 rupees to promote the job ad. discussion about using rohan's card for payment. yogita had trouble adding her card initially, but it was resolved. confirmation that the amount was deducted and the ad was posted. discussion of pausing the job ad due to concerns about unqualified applicants. need to confirm how sohan set up the job ad to avoid unqualified applications. emphasis on the importance of attracting relevant candidates. discussion of checking the 'careers at pf' page for potential applicants.", "data scraping and analysis - initial discussion: aryan dev describes using node.js to generate 1000-1500 fake data points for a sql project (instagram database analytics). chayan roy asks about handling actual data, prompting a discussion about web scraping and apis for instagram data. aryan dev mentions using the 'inspect column' method to filter details from data. chayan roy clarifies that he's not asking aryan dev to build an api, but to discuss how to work with actual datasets. aryan dev admits limited experience with apis, primarily focusing on data science and machine learning. both discuss using kaggle datasets for practice, but acknowledge the need to work with real-world data from web scraping and apis. chayan roy expresses interest in aryan dev gaining experience with real datasets. aryan dev suggests that obtaining real data typically involves web scraping and api calls. they discuss the importance of scraping websites like instagram to gather data for analysis.", "gtm strategy & market research - initial guidance to harsh: