elers. discussion of the account containing real-world data with variances, allowing ayush to practice data analysis skills. the account will be used to analyze data related to user behavior, engagement, and conversions. rohan emphasizes the importance of confirming theoretical knowledge with real-world data. the real account is intended to provide ayush with a practical learning experience. discussion of using the account to explore data related昕 to travel data plans and user behavior.", "data scraping & analysis process: chayan explained the data scraping process involves automating data extraction from competitor websites. the scraping system is designed to run automatically every 2-3 days. the data is considered useless if it's not analyzed and used to gain insights. the company emphasizes the importance of data analysis after scraping. data analysis is considered a crucial part of the process. the company focuses on extracting meaningful insights from the data. the company utilizes data analysis to improve decision-making. the company uses data analysis to identify trends and opportunities. the company uses data analysis to track performance and measure success. the company uses data analysis to optimize processes and improve efficiency. the company believes that data analysis is essential for staying ahead of the competition.", "dashboard creation & data focus: rohan stresses the importance of thinking through the dashboard layout and data tables. focus on social media dashboard first, then e-commerce. rohan emphasizes the need to understand how data is used and presented. discussion of isha and ayush's work on data pipelines. rohan highlights the importance of documentation for future use with llms. emphasis on capturing quality thoughts in a structured way. rohan acknowledges he hasn't had time to review the documentation properly. harsh will be given access to documentation spaces. importance of understanding the current projects and data pipelines. rohan encourages harsh to ask questions and identify mistakes in the documentation. discussion of google analytics dashboards, core concepts, and reports. focus on ensuring data accuracy and identifying trends.", "front-end progress & google analytics documentation: rohan inquired about the status of the front-end work. aditya confirmed the front-end work isn't yet completed but will be finished by tomorrow evening. aditya is currently documenting google analytics, focusing on acquisition reports (lead, non-google campaign, user). ayush offered to review aditya's google analytics documentation after the night stand-up (either 9:30 pm or 11 pm, depending on ayush’s schedule). rohan requested a review of the documentation to correct any misunderstandings. discussion about the timing of the review, factoring in ayush's stand-up meetings. confirmation of the review time as either 9:30 pm or 11 pm. mention of retention and monetization reports as next steps for google analytics documentation. the review aims to ensure clarity and accuracy of the google analytics documentation. the documentation is crucial for understanding data acquisition and user behavior.", "ai project discussion & research (esha, rohan): rohan suggests esha can start researching ai projects concurrently with the dashboard work. this will provide a natural break from the dashboard creation and allow for focused research. the goal is to have clarity on the ai project direction by the time the dashboard work is complete. esha will focus on understanding the data and potential ai applications. rohan requests esha to provide updates on the ai project research during stand-up meetings. he wants to understand the rationale behind the chosen project and the research approach. the emphasis is on proactive communication and transparency regarding the ai project. esha is encouraged to explore data science-related projects and predictive analysis. there's a willingness to provide guidance and support for the ai project research.", "data extraction progress & challenges: chayan roy extracted data for 14-15 companies out of 53, using gemini. chayan roy mentioned challenges with adaptive crawling. aryan pal was preparing to show his data extraction work. discussion about data accuracy and the need for confirmation. chayan roy explained gemini's approach of extracting data only with 100% certainty. aryan pal asked if rohan had reviewed the dashboard. rohan confirmed he would share his dashboards as well. discussion about the importance of random data checks for verification. chayan roy detailed using gemini for data extraction and the limitations encountered. aryan pal inquired about the dashboard review status. the team discussed the process of verifying extracted data for accuracy.", "data extraction & api challenges: rohan and isha discuss the complexities of extracting data from apis. isha expresses difficulty understanding business definitions related to the data. isha feels she's spending too much time on business context and not enough on technical skills. isha is concerned about the lack of practical application of her pipeline knowledge. rohan highlights the importance of understanding how business utilizes the data. isha questions how the current data work will help her career goals. isha feels overwhelmed by the volume of information and lacks clarity on its application. rohan emphasizes the need to understand kpis at different levels (l1, l2, l3). discussion on the value of understanding the 'why' behind the data, not just the 'how'. isha questions the future value of understanding business context in the age of ai. rohan suggests that understanding business context will be more valuable than technical skills in the long run. isha asks about the possibility of focusing on the technical aspects while someone else handles the business context. rohan acknowledges isha's concerns but reiterates the importance of having a holistic understanding. isha is confused about how the 