rtance of understanding the project and being able to answer basic questions. the goal is to transition the new hire into a position where they can lead stand-up meetings independently. discussion of the onboarding process and the importance of clear communication.", "stand-up time adjustment discussion: gayatri suggested moving the stand-up time earlier to 10:15 am. reasoning: yogita works late, and an earlier stand-up would allow her more sleep. harsh sharma suggested using the 11:00 am slot for a growth-specific stand-up. harsh will create a new meeting invite for the 11:00 am growth stand-up. discussion about the benefits of an earlier stand-up to avoid feeling rushed. harsh proposed restarting his operation stand-up at 11:00 am. the team will consider the suggestion and decide if they want to move the stand-up time.", "scheduling & logistics: rohan informs the team that the morning stand-up tomorrow will be delayed due to a factory visit. rohan requests yogita and harsh to share the dashboard draft with him if they can't meet tomorrow. the team plans to discuss the dashboard further on monday. discussion of setting up a call after noon tomorrow to continue the dashboard discussion.", "intern content creation & skill assessment: gayatri requests yogita to provide writing references from sakina and other decent interns. the focus is on assessing the interns' content creation skills. gayatri is seeking to identify interns who can produce quality content. the conversation suggests a need to evaluate the interns' writing abilities. yogita is tasked with identifying interns with potential for content creation. the discussion implies a desire to improve the quality of content created by the interns.", "yogita's health & stand-up availability: yogita states she is not feeling well. yogita is unsure if she can attend the morning stand-up. yogita anticipates being able to connect with rohan in the afternoon. she expresses her best effort to connect. this highlights poten