ight' post, gathering preferences from vedika, samira, and viraj.\\n  • vedika can contribute ideas and reference materials for ugc content creative direction, but doesn't need to be the editor.\\n  • yogita will set up a call with manish and rohan to discuss the packaging video and in-house image creation capabilities.\\n  • viraj will generate a visual for the first post based on the team's feedback.\\n  • viraj will create visuals for a skincare campaign, inspired by a cocktail/perfume concept but adapted to desserts.\\n  • vedika will share brands she's researched. gayatri will start by presenting good weather skin, 52 sundays, and secret alchemist.\\n  • the team will wait for vedika's suggestions for women's day content.\\n  • vedika will share a specific post (from another brand) on mattermost with a description for reference regarding travel-size packaging and layering concepts.\\n  • explore potential collaborations with ngos, co-ops, and artists who align with the brand's values. vedika will research and document these for future consideration.\\n  • vedika will focus on hula hoop stories for trend analysis.\\n\\n⚠️ Open Concerns:\\n  • need for clear communication and collaboration between ishneet and gayatri.\\n  • harsh's initial understanding of the project and team workflows.\\n  • potential delays if harsh sharma encounters roadblocks while building functionalities.\\n  • dependence on harsh sharma to build functionalities, potentially creating a bottleneck.\\n  • none explicitly stated, but there is an implicit concern about finding suitable content or talent.\\n  • pressure to generate enough content options.\\n  • ensuring harsh feels supported and has opportunities for growth.\\n  • dependence on yashpal completing the photo upload before proceeding with other tasks.\\n  • need to ensure content is visually appealing and engaging.\\n  • the importance of incorporating siddhant's feedback on ad copy.\\n  • ensuring all team members are aligned on 