ersion rates within a 24-hour window.\\n16. The team acknowledged the need to differentiate between high conversion rates due to user intent versus website strength.\\n17. Rohan will update the cohort definition to focus on session and conversion patterns.\\n18. Rohan will remove or adjust the 'a and b' factors in the cohort definition.\\n19. The team will critically evaluate Chat GPT outputs and verify information whenever possible.\\n20. They will question assumptions and investigate explanations that seem 'too good'.\\n21. Rohan will look for data supporting the idea of distinct user cohorts (paid, organic, direct) based on psychological state.\\n22. The team will investigate if there's research on differences in user behavior based on acquisition channel (paid vs. organic).\\n23. They will consider the impact of brand establishment on organic traffic conversion rates (higher for established brands, potentially lower for new brands).\\n24. The team decided to verify if there's data on the psychological state of users from different acquisition channels.\\n25. Rohan and Ayush will proceed with a detailed review of the documentation, one item per day, starting tomorrow.\\n26. Rohan will consider introducing hands-on exercises or projects for Ayush after two to three months.\\n27. Rohan will think about introducing something new for Ayush to work on starting next week.\\n28. Rohan aims to build Ayush's confidence so he doesn't need to constantly check Ayush's work after the initial period.\\n29. Agreement to prioritize building a strong foundation of knowledge even if it takes longer (two to four months).\\n30. Rohan will focus on ensuring Ayush can differentiate between valid and invalid information, especially when it 'sounds logical'.\\n31. Rohan will provide Ayush with real-world tasks as early as next month.\\n\\n================================================================================\\n✅ ACTION ITEMS\\n==================================================