s exploring the potential of ai to automate tasks and improve workflows. chayan is responsible for researching and evaluating ai skills.", "ai-powered front-end creation & automation: discussion of using ai skills (cloud skills) to automate content creation, specifically for creating visual front-ends from markdown documents. exploring the use of ai agents to transform markdown into visually appealing front-ends with diagrams and details. mention of librechat agent as a potential starting point for this automation. questioning whether cloud skills can be used with personal api keys or only within the cloud skills platform. chayan will research using cloud skills with ulama on his own pc. discussion of automating report generation from open-source projects (e.g., github scraping). the team acknowledges a need for more fit interns to dedicate time to these projects. focus on converting interview candidates to increase team capacity. exploration of using ai to create dynamic content and visualizations. emphasis on the potential of ai to improve content delivery and user experience. discussion of the challenges of creating consistent results with ai models. chayan mentioned the importance of version control with open-source models to maintain consistent performance.", "image classification & clip model: rohan kumar mentioned finding clip as an image classifier. discussion of whether automation tools or orchestrators are needed for image classification. clip is described as a zero-shot image classifier model. rohan kumar suggests testing clip before committing to more complex solutions. chayan roy asks if anyone is interested in working with image classifier models. rohan kumar suggests initially keeping the image classification project small and self-contained. decision to involve the team later, after initial testing and validation. rohan kumar wants to create a project and ask for volunteers once the initial work is done. the goal is to explore image classification wi