================\\n📚 HISTORICAL CONTEXT\\n================================================================================\\n\\n🧠 Prior Decisions:\\n  • chayan roy will present his project progress (structure and current build) for review, with a scheduled meeting to be determined based on rohan kumar and the team's availability.\\n  • chayan roy will prioritize setting up a ci/cd pipeline with gitlab, aiming for automated code deployment nightly.\\n  • chayan roy will onboard a new team member, prioritizing giving them working resources to start with.\\n  • chayan will work with dhruvik to fill out a sheet detailing requirements for the image classification project.\\n  • rohan will discuss user journey patterns with chayan roy tomorrow.\\n  • the team will assess shubhang's suitability for collaboration based on observations and feedback from chayan roy and aditya raj.\\n  • chayan roy will share access to the container or vm with isha for running the data processing models.\\n  • rohan will share the link to the design stand-up meeting (shared on mattermost).\\n  • rohan and dhruvik will connect before the evening stand-up to discuss dashboards.\\n  • rohan will share access to necessary tools/platforms with yashpal.\\n  • rohan will connect with someone from the design team once the mvp of the 'pf.grow supercharged' dashboard is live.\\n  • rohan and harsh are collaborating on a dashboard, with rohan explaining the logic and data points used.\\n  • rohan will connect with yashpal and faisal to understand their availability for uploading images and address any issues.\\n\\n⚠️ Open Concerns:\\n  • the importance of incorporating siddhant's feedback on ad copy.\\n  • ensuring radhika addresses the label issue promptly.\\n  • aligning sahil's skills with pristyn care's diverse design approach.\\n  • ensuring harsh has a clear understanding of the requirements for the dashboard template.\\n  • ensuring sahil understands the pristyn care brand aesthetic before starting any work.\\n  • potential for miscommunication or lack of clarity during the onboarding process.\\n  • ensuring harsh feels supported and has access to necessary information.\\n  • ensuring proper coordination between rohan and yashpal.\\n  • need for clear communication and collaboration between ishneet and gayatri.\\n  • the possibility of something suspicious causing email filtering (though rohan believes it's unlikely).\\n  • the importance of clear communication between rohan and varun.\\n  • dependence on yashpal completing the photo upload before proceeding with other tasks.\\n  • need to ensure correct user profiles in mattermost.\\n\\n📋 Related Action Items:\\n  • chayan roy to chayan roy to set up ci/ அம்சங்கள் cd pipeline with gitlab. by ASAP\\n  • chayan roy to update changes in the night stand-up by Night stand-up\\n  • chayan roy to chayan roy to onboard a new team member. by ASAP\\n  • chayan roy to chayan roy to determine which ai model can best distinguish between product images. by Not specified\\n  • chayan roy/team (initially chayan roy) to explore clip image classifier model. by Within one day (implied)\\n  • chayan roy to explore gitlab or github interface versions for ci/cd, considering cost. by next week\\n  • dhruvik bamniya to share tar files with chayan roy. by Immediately\\n  • rohan kumar & dhruvik bamniya to rohan and dhruvik to connect before evening stand-up to discuss dashboards. by Before evening stand-up\\n  • rohan kumar to rohan to share the dashboard with asia after feedback. by unspecified\\n  • rohan kumar to rohan to connect with harsh separately for 15 minutes to discuss onboarding. by Unspecified\\n  • rohan kumar to follow up with ahilya after the stand-up. by After 6:30-7:00 stand-up\\n  • harsh sharma to connect with rohan to discuss data visualization and parameter naming. by Today\\n  • rohan kumar and chayan roy to discuss user journey patterns. by tomorrow\\n  • rohan kumar to rohan to review harsh's experience with social media data analysis. by immediately\\n\\n================================================================================\\n📝 MEETING SUMMARY (BY TOPIC)\\n================================================================================\\n\\n[00:40 - 03:47] 📌 RAG System & Data Scraping from GitHub\\n  • Aditya is developing a RAG system and exploring the GitHub API.\\n  • The goal is to capture project data from GitHub, including forks, commit dates, and project information.\\n  • The GitHub API has a rate limit of 60 requests per hour.\\n  • Aditya plans to use LLMs for initial detection of generic projects and anomaly detection (e.g., projects committed in one day are flagged).\\n  • Isha will be involved in building ML models to classify projects as generated or genuine, potentially after the LLM phase.\\n  • Discussion about using the data for detecting fraudulent or copied projects.\\n  • Consideration of using LLMs for ICL (In-Context Learning) due to the potential for new medical doctors contributing projects.\\n  • Data will be used to identify trending projects.\\n  • Discussion on the need for a database to store generic projects.\\n  • The system will aim to detect anomalies in project commit history.\\n  • Isha's involvement will increase as she's also working on the dashboard view.\\n\\n[03:57 - 05:53] 📌 Dockerization & Backend Deployment\\n  • Shubham is dockerizing the backend.\\n  • There's a delay in loading the task page.\\n  • The plan is to deploy the dockerized backend directly to the server.\\n  • Guinish has been messaged for a meeting report, but hasn't replied yet.\\n  • Once deployed, the team will start using the new backend.\\n  • Discussion about the functionality needed in the manager page.\\n\\n[05:54 - 09:05] 📌 Manager Page Functionality & Task Management\\n  • Shubham outlines the desired functionality for the manager page.\\n  • Managers need a view of tasks assigned to each team member.\\n  • Ability to see the status of ta