 on nano and micro-influencers for potential collaborations. discussion of barter collaborations vs. commercial deals. analysis of influencer profiles (followers, reach, content quality). discussion of influencer content (english language, skincare/beauty focus). yogita describing the qualities of potential influencers (soma, navneet, sapna). discussion of the influencer's content and its alignment with the brand. discussion of influencer rates (1500-2000 for a deal). emphasis on ugc (user-generated content) and human element in content. yogita describing the content of an influencer (sapna) and her focus on real reviews. discussion of influencer content and its impact on product focus. yogita's observation about an influencer's eyes and its impact on content focus. confirmation of the need to gather market rates for influencer collaborations.", "influencer identification & evaluation: gayatri found an influencer with a connection to the indian movement and delhi capital. discussion about whether the influencer's previous brand affiliations align with their brand. yogita asks if sameera has added new influencers. yogita requests sameera to text her when new influencers are added. concern about an influencer having only 7 posts, but a substantial video library. discussion about influencers removing content from their grid but maintaining videos. yogita suggests exploring influencers with a similar aesthetic to their brand. yogita suggests adding both nano and micro-influencers. discussion about influencer reach and engagement. yogita and sameera discuss the number of influencers to add (aiming for around 20).", "content calendar progress & influencer outreach: yogita checked intern content and sent emails. yogita will reach out to more influencers today. discussion about adding an extension to an email. yogita was unable to connect with harsh due to other commitments. yogita will connect with harsh tomorrow after he's worked on the data. discussion about the progress of the content calendar. mariam and samira connected during the stand-up. they reviewed brands the team is following and the content calendar progress. gayatri provided feedback on keeping records of brand activity and post ideas. the team is working on documenting brand activity for future reference.", "yogita's influencer outreach and content calendar progress: y水igita reports sending emails to potential content writer interns. she's reviewing submitted work and expects more by 8 pm. she plans to interview 2-3 people for the intern positions. yogita has reached out to 10-12 influencers. some influencers are interested in paid collaborations and have standard rates. she'll share details with interested influencers after the design stand-up. yogita had a call with the interns regarding the content calendar. they aim to complete 80% of the next 17 days' content by tomorrow. remaining content will focus on women's day posts, expected to be completed by thursday. discussion about social media research – monitoring brands' posts for inspiration. focus is currently on story content, as other posts are often ugc or short-form. they are gathering ideas for the content calendar. yogita is looking for the interns to manage specific posts to gain experience.", "influencer & ugc outreach strategy & documentation: yogita has created a document outlining the influencer outreach strategy. the document includes details on how to approach influencers and track progress. yogita has also shared login credentials for relevant tools. yogita will ask samira to create outreach messages to assess her understanding. discussion of finalizing the list of influencers and starting the outreach process. yogita shared example outreach messages with rohan for guidance. discussion of the strategy for ugc (user-generated content) outreach. emphasis on documentation and clear processes for influencer and ugc outreach. the team is focused on ensuring samira understands the outreach process. rohan is providing guidance on the outreach messaging. the team is actively working on finalizing the influencer list and starting the outreach. there's a clear strategy in place for both influencer and ugc acquisition.", "content creation & alignment: rohan mentioning his work on content creation and checking intern content. rohan adding references for ruchi and radhika's posts due to creative misalignment. discussion of influencer responses and potential collaborations. yogita sharing updates on influencer outreach. discussion of the need to create a list of influencers, their commercial rates, and profiles. emphasis on ugc (user-generated content) and human element in content. discussion of content quality and its alignment with the brand. discussion of the need to create content that resonates with the target audience.", "stand-up meeting recap: the stand-up meeting involved mariam and samira. they discussed brands being followed and the content calendar progress. gayatri provided feedback on tracking brand activities and post ideas. the team will document brand activities for future reference. the stand-up focused on progress and feedback related to the content calendar.", "content creation & caption review: sameera has made changes to the content based on previous discussions. yogita will review the content and provide feedback. discussion of a specific content piece involving 'baked into memory' and ingredients. gayatri describes creating captions for a six-frame content piece. the captions focus on three ingredients and an unforgettable body oil. emphasis on crafting captions that evoke a sensory experience. discussion of the tone and style of the captions. yogita will review the captions to ensure they align with the brand's voice. gayatri and sameera discuss the progress of content creation. they are working to create visually appealing and engaging content.", "brand inspiration & content benchmarking: discussion of various brands for content inspiration (sangre shooter, brands with giveaways like madam and john jacobs). focus on visual aesthetics and production value of competitor brands. exploration of brands with ai-generated content vs. bestellung photoshoots. brands discussed: sangre shooter, various brands with giveaways, a band with candles and soaps, a band with a white woman aesthetic, several unnamed bands. emphasis on regularly posting content as a key characteristic of inspiring brands. discussion of color palettes and alignment with the team's aesthetic. viraj and gayatri presenting brands they found. yogita suggesting brands to add to the list. discussion of whether to add brands that don't fully align with the aesthetic but might offer valuable inspiration. sharing of links to brand pages for review. focus on finding brands that post regularly. brands being added to a shared list for future reference. discussion on whether to add brands even if they don't fully align with the aesthetic. brands were evaluated based on production value and aesthetic appeal. the team was looking for brands that regularly post content.", "reddit community building & influencer outreach: rohan proposes activating skincare/self-care enthusiasts from other subreddits to join pristyn forest. the plan involves offering samples in exchange for ugc feedback. rohan asks dhruvik to collaborate with mariam on this initiative. dhruvik's role is to provide feedback on mariam's planning, not to lead. rohan will guide mariam during the 8 pm stand-ups. discussion of expanding community building efforts beyond reddit. exploration of organic engagement strategies, not just paid advertising. rohan emphasizes finding ways to bring enthusiasts together. the goal is to create a thriving community around pristyn forest. focus on leveraging user-generated content to build trust and authenticity.", "content refinement: 'smells like...' post (body mist): detailed discussion and refinement of a content idea for a body mist post, initially titled 'what does