tinue working on the remaining tasks. yogita and gayatri will focus on selecting images for the pdp. rohan will share a detailed ingredient list with yogita and gayatri. the team will collaborate to finalize the images and upload them to the website. rohan emphasized the importance of clear communication and coordination. discussion of the need for yashpal and faisal to connect with the team. rohan will follow up with yashpal and faisal to schedule a call. the team will work together to ensure that the website content is finalized and uploaded on time. clarification on the roles and responsibilities of each team member. emphasis on the importance of teamwork and collaboration. the team discussed the challenges of finalizing website content and the need for effective communication.", "content creation details & visual elements (face mist, body mist, ingredients): discussion about adding one-line content to each slide, focusing on benefits or key features. viraj suggests adding alternative content options for review. emphasis on avoiding product overlap – ensuring different products are highlighted each week. discussion of visual elements for specific products (face mist, body mist). viraj describes planned visual transitions (e.g., desert scene to rose garden). connection between visual elements and product ingredients (e.g., roses pérdidas in face mist). request for viraj to rework the content based on feedback. discussion of the need for high-quality visuals and consistent branding. yogita and vedika are reviewing and approving content. emphasis on visual storytelling and conveying the brand's message. content is being created for instagram posts, not just images but also reels.", "content review & next steps: gayatri asks yogita to review the feed and provide feedback. gayatri plans to discuss content with rohan and provide an update. yogita agrees to review the feed. the conversation indicates a desire to finalize content plans. the discussion suggests a collaborative approach to content creation. the conversation concludes with a confirmation of next steps and a thank you.", "project prioritization & weekly goals for harsh: harsh's p0 for the week is dashboards: social media, main dashboard, and individual department dashboards. harsh is expected to deliver a v1 draft of the social media dashboard as soon as possible. once the v1 draft is ready, rohan will involve isha and provide feedback. harsh will then be assigned the artist collaboration project, with rohan providing guidance on future development. rohan emphasizes the importance of understanding the task flow and replicating it across projects. harsh is expected to work on circular logistics, artist collaboration, second bloom, and membership programs as recurring projects. 竜王 estimates these recurring projects will take 2-3 months to fully flesh out. rohan requests a recap from harsh to confirm understanding of expectations. emphasis on delivering a complete and well-defined dashboard, not just a starting point. the goal is to create a dashboard that others can build upon and extend. harsh will be responsible for defining key metrics and kpis for the dashboards. harsh is expected to collaborate with isha on dashboard development. rohan wants harsh to focus on understanding the overall project flow and replicating it across different areas. discussion about the timeline for completing the recurring projects and the level of detail required.", "onboarding & stand-up meetings: rohan plans to have harsh shadow stand-up meetings for the first one or two months. the goal is for harsh to learn the process and eventually lead the stand-up meetings independently. rohan suggests a separate 15-minute connect with harsh to discuss the onboarding process. harsh will be able to choose whether to listen in or drop off during the stand-up meetings. rohan emphasizes the benefits of observing the stand-up meetings to gain a better understanding of the project. rohan wants harsh to understand the project context and be able to answer basic questions. discussion of the daily stand-up schedule (11:15 am). rohan is thinking about the new operations guy and how to integrate them into the stand-up process.", "women's day content planning & delegation: discussion of the lack of progress on the women's day reel and post. delegation of the task to vedika to provide ideas and direction. acknowledgment that the existing women's day posts are simple and lack creativity. agreement to wait for vedika's input before proceeding with the women's day content. discussion of the lack of progress on the women's day reel and post. delegation of the task to vedika to provide ideas and direction. acknowledgment that the existing women's day posts are simple and lack creativity. agreement to wait for vedika's input before proceeding with the women's day content.", "visual content & reference gathering: yogita reviewed ngo story ideas and liked one, requesting more context. feedback on holy post ideas: one was too ai-heavy, the other product-focused. request for better references for holy and ngo posts. discussion of using real-life shots instead of ai-generated images. emphasis on tagging ids in the content calendar sheet to indicate preferred shots. request to prioritize shooting real-life shots whenever possible. discussion of visual references for world wildlife day. yogita highlights the importance of high-quality visuals. discussion of visual inspiration from brands like brave beauty, herbivore, fragrant oats, and mel talk. discussion on current trends in visual content, such as product shots on bathroom shelves.", "women's day & holy post ideation: the primary outstanding task is to generate ideas for both women's day and holy posts. maryam and viraj previously presented two ideas for the holy post. sameera expressed uncertainty about whether the previously presented holy post ideas will receive approval. there's a desire to explore additional ideas for both women's day and holy posts, even with existing concepts. the team plans to meet the following day to brainstorm and finalize content ideas. the discussion implies a need for multiple options to increase the likelihood of approval. the conversation suggests a collaborative approach to content ideation. there is an implicit understanding that content needs to be created in advance to meet deadlines. the discussion is brief, indicating the topic is a follow-up from previous discussions or a quick check-in. the team is proactively planning for upcoming holidays and events."]}, "sentiment_analysis": {"score": 0.5, "overall": "neutral", "negative_indicators": 3, "positive_indicators": 3}}, "metadata": {"date": "2026-02-12", "title": "Social & Content Team Standup", "participants": ["Gayatri Ramdas", "Maryam Fatima", "Sameera Parveen", "Viraj Kanojia", "Yogita Nagpal"], "transcript_path": "/root/transcriptor/meetingassistant/transcripts/merged/2026-02-12_17-30_social-content-team-standup__meet-recording-c26e027e-add5-4e12-9e23-f472ff47dff6.json", "duration_minutes": 50}, "video_url": "http://pfvideos.growthsupercharged.com/web/index.html#!/details?id=a6456185841556a7abb2e97799d9fb62", "generated_at": "2026-02-12T13:21:21.192924", "formatted_report": "================================================================================\\n🧠 MEETING ANALYSIS REPORT\\n================================================================================\\n\\n📋 Title: Social & Content Team Standup\\n📅 Date: 2026-02-12\\n⏱️ Duration: 50 minutes\\n👥 Participants: Gayatri Ramdas, Maryam Fatima, Sameera Parveen, Viraj Kanojia, Yogita Nagpal\\n\\n================================================================================\\n📚 HISTORICAL CONTEXT\\n================================================================================\\n\\n🧠 Prior Decisions:\\n  • yogita will send details to influencers and follow up on barter collaborations.\\n  • yogita will follow up with influencers today.\\n  • yo