with other projects and justification for the selection. rohan emphasizes the need for thorough documentation for future reference. akarshhan mentions the cms's ability to work with sql databases directly. the cms is designed to be ui-first.", "commercial discussion & budget: rohan outlines a budget range of 15k-35k per month for ugc content creation. they've previously onboarded creators at both ends of this range. they are aiming for a six-month contract, potentially extending to a longer term. the desired contract value is around 1.8-2 lakh for 60 videos. nourish nurture initially expresses a preference for 5k per asset. rohan explains the need for high-quality assets and the desire to own them. they discuss the possibility of a three-month initial contract. nourish nurture indicates willingness to consider a longer-term collaboration. rohan clarifies that the budget is constrained due to being a startup. there's a discussion about the equipment used for content creation (phone vs. dslr). rohan mentions previous negotiations with other creators and the challenges of balancing budget and quality. nourish nurture expresses understanding of the startup's financial constraints. rohan proposes a potential compromise for a three-month period.", "data collection for production failures (airflow, dbt, airbyte): esha joshi described collecting 90+ production failures from github repositories using airflow, dbt, and airbyte. the data includes url, tools used, issue title, log snippet, and github link. discussion about whether to include data from other platforms like stack overflow. esha joshi described the data format and the types of information collected. focus on cleaning and structuring the messy data using llama 3 or openai api. the goal is to generate 500+ labeled data points from the initial 90. discussion about using a gpu for data cleaning and processing. mention of scheduling the process at night to run the data cleaning pipeline. esha joshi asked for assistance with gpu access and integration of the api endpoints. discussion of the data scraping strategy and the use of personal authorization tokens.", "daily stand-up & meeting logistics: discussion of daily stand-up meetings and their schedules (11:15 am, 6:00 pm, 8:00 pm). harsh's unavailability today and rescheduling of connection for setup. rohan mentioning harsh will connect tomorrow. confirmation of the growth stand-up schedule and harsh's potential attendance. discussion of the daily routine and the importance of stand-up meetings for updates. rohan outlining the daily routine, including the two core stand-up meetings. mention of separate tech stand-ups due to departmental differences. discussion of integrating new hires into the stand-up process. rohan's plan for harsh to shadow stand-up meetings initially. goal of transitioning harsh to independently lead stand-up meetings. emphasis on clear communication during the onboarding process. r맵han's plan to share the dashboard with asia after feedback. discussion of the need to solve issues with accessing recordings on jellyfin. suggestion to explore meetings directly through the chatbot on mattermost. yogita confirming harsh's update about his unavailability.", "data cleaning and preparation - esha's progress: esha is cleaning and normalizing process data, focusing on job ids, ip addresses, and timestamps. the goal is to prepare the dataset for intelligence layer application. esha anticipates completing the cleaning and descriptive analysis within the next day or two. esha will present the cleaned dataset during the next night stand-up. esha is currently running a model and will proceed with cleaning after it completes. esha will perform descriptive analysis to understand the data after cleaning. esha is working on the normalization step to clean the data. esha is focusing on preparing the dataset for applying an intelligence layer. the model is currently running, and cleaning will follow. descriptive analysis will be 