t Development - Shaving Category\\n  • Discussion centered around developing a shaving product line for men, specifically focusing on pre-shave and aftershave oils, lotions, and potentially beard oil.\\n  • Seema Samanta shared research on existing brands like Pink Wolf and Leather Shave Company, detailing ingredients, variants, and pricing.\\n  • Rohan Kumar emphasized the importance of considering manufacturing processes, similar to how they approached solid perfumes.\\n  • They discussed the possibility of offering a shaving kit with multiple products, but Rohan cautioned against starting with a comprehensive kit, suggesting they focus on individual products first.\\n  • Rohan stressed the need to identify a factory capable of producing the formulations and sourcing essential oils.\\n  • There was a debate on whether to prioritize a full kit or individual products, with Rohan advocating for starting with the basics and adding combos later.\\n  • Rohan suggested focusing on pre-shave and aftershave oils initially, potentially adding lotion and beard oil later.\\n  • The discussion touched on packaging - specifically using smaller bottles (10-15ml) for oils to encourage repeat purchases.\\n  • Rohan highlighted the importance of considering the Minimum Order Quantity (MOQ) and sourcing of materials.\\n  • They discussed the possibility of offering different product formats, such as oil, lotion, and mist.\\n  • The conversation included a comparison of Indian and global brands and their pricing strategies.\\n  • Rohan mentioned the need to assess market size and growth potential before prioritizing specific product categories.\\n  • Seema Samanta offered to research market size, CAGR, and pricing data for the shaving category.\\n  • Rohan suggested creating separate tabs for each product category (pre-shave, aftershave, lotion, beard oil) to organize research.\\n  • The discussion included a consideration of offering solid perfumes alongside the वांछित shaving produ