earch the API documentation and provide layman's terms explanations of the events.\\n  • The project aims to automate the process of finding and understanding API events, reducing manual effort and improving efficiency.\\n  • A future phase of the project could involve recommending ad strategies based on data analysis, but the initial focus is on accessing and understanding the documentation.\\n  • Rohan Kumar acknowledged the abstract nature of the problem and the need for further exploration.\\n  • The project will involve creating a system that can understand business definitions and map them to relevant API events.\\n  • Rohan will spend a day researching potential solutions and provide feedback by tomorrow evening's stand-up.\\n  • The discussion highlighted the challenge of managing a large and complex API landscape.\\n  • Akarshhan described the current process as time-consuming and inefficient.\\n  • The proposed solution aims to simplify the process and empower users to easily access and understand the API documentation.\\n  • The project will involve building a system that can understand natural language business definitions and translate them into technical API queries.\\n  • The project could potentially leverage large language models to understand the meaning of API events and provide explanations in plain language.\\n  • The long-term goal is to create a self-service platform that empowers users to easily access and utilize the API data.\\n\\n[26:10 - 29:41] 📌 RN Google Account Pressure & New Dev Onboarding\\n  👥 Key participants: Chayan Roy\\n  • Chayan Roy inquired about the status of a 'pressure' issue related to an RN Google account.\\n  • He mentioned he hasn't received a reply regarding this issue.\\n  • Chayan mentioned a new developer ('RN') will be joining tomorrow.\\n  • This new developer is facing some issues, which Chayan will connect with them about tomorrow.\\n  • The discussion was brief and focused on logistical updates.\\n  • Chayan i