scripts.", "harsh sharma requests completion of an unspecified task by tonight's growth stand-up meeting.", "gayatri suggested using ai to generate content ideas for the coming week, noting a shift in brand approaches towards raw and organic content.", "aditya and shubhang can drop off after discussing the website discussion.", "sameera and viraj will also be connected, potentially in the evening, to<unused1629> discuss content.", "gayatri ramdas concluded the meeting after rohan's confirmation and a general check for further topics.", "rohan kumar will research a solution for akarshhan's api documentation/event definition problem and provide an update by tomorrow evening's stand-up.", "rohan will provide sanjeev with a timeline for project completion, allowing flexibility for research and design.", "rohan kumar will continue working on carousel posts and explore the possibility of creating reels in the future, but will prioritize carousels for now.", "rohit kundhiya will draft questions for the grant and email them to rohan for review.", "rohan will finalize influencer marketing guidelines and a legal contract, seeking assistance from previous colleagues if needed.", "rohan will confirm if he can joinfuncname stand-ups and share updates.", "犢 harsh will connect with isha and ask for updates, and rohan will join the call to provide feedback.", "犢 harsh will connect with isha to understand dashboard progress and provide guidance.", "the team decided to define 'volatility' as a kpi within the google sheet.", "rohan will share shopify dashboard access with ayush for the 8 pm stand-up."], "meeting_segments": ["general check-in & follow-ups: rohan kumar asked if anyone wanted to discuss anything before concluding the meeting. aryan pal requested rohan to ask ahilya to connect. rohan kumar mentioned that ahilya will likely be available after 7 pm due to a stand-up meeting. rohan kumar mentioned he will update changes in the night stand-up. brief check-in to ensure all topics were covered and any outstanding questions were addressed. rohan mentioned he just returned from college. confirmation that the night stand-up will be a follow-up point for further discussion. general housekeeping to wrap up the meeting and ensure everyone is aligned. rohan asked for any final thoughts or questions from the team. confirmation of the next steps and follow-up actions. rohan mentioned messaging last week and ensuring things were in place. rohan confirming a connection around 3:30 with yes.", "growth project & skill development: rohan mentioned a growth-related project starting in 1-2 days. aditya can either take a break or learn google ads while waiting for the project. aditya is currently going through a google ads tutorial. chayan roy intends to finish up with guinness after this discussion.", "daily stand-up & team availability: discussion of the 8 o'clock stand-up with ayush. rohan mentions his grandmother being admitted to the hospital. rohan plans to attend the 8:30 call from his phone if possible. harsh offers support and understanding. rohan will inform ayush about his situation and potential absence. the team is coordinating schedules and ensuring coverage during the stand-up.", "daily stand-up & personal circumstances: confirmation of the 8 o'clock stand-up meeting with ayush. rohan mentions his grandmother's hospitalization and potential need to leave the stand-up. agreement that rohan can skip the stand-up if necessary. rohan plans to attend the stand-up with his parents present. discussion of the possibility of rohan asking a colleague about an ndn sla. confirmation of sharing the stand-up link with ayush.", "daily stand-up meetings & scheduling: discussion of daily stand-up meetings and their schedules (11:15 am, 6:00 pm, 8:00 pm). harsh's unavailability today and rescheduling of connection for setup. rohan mentioning harsh will connect tomorrow. confirmation of the growth stand-up schedule and harsh's potential attendance. discussion of the daily routine and the importance of stand-up meetings for updates. rohan outlining the daily routine, including the two core stand-up meetings. mention of separate tech stand-ups due to departmental differences. discussion of integrating new hires into the stand-up process. rohan's plan for harsh to shadow stand-up meetings initially. goal of transitioning harsh to independently lead stand-up meetings. emphasis on clear communication during the onboarding process. rohan's plan to share the dashboard with asia after feedback. discussion of the need to solve issues with accessing recordings on jellyfin. suggestion to explore meetings directly through the chatbot on mattermost. yogita confirming harsh's update about his unavailability.", "general project updates & stand-up mentions: mention of sandeep's ongoing project and potential updates during stand-up meetings. dhruvik will start taking updates in the stand-up meetings in a couple of weeks. sandeep is working on redesigning ui/ux for internal dashboards and a consultancy tool. yogita encourages participation in the 6:30-7:00 pm calls.", "mariam's absence/joining status: rohan kumar inquired about mariam's absence. seema samanta indicated mariam was supposed to join today. seema samanta expressed uncertainty about mariam's actual joining date, mentioning she thought it was the 19th. seema samanta noted mariam is expected to join the other stand-up meeting. the discussion is a quick check on mariam’s onboarding status and attendance at meetings.", "market research & prioritization: rohan kumar and seema samanta discussed the importance of conducting market research to identify the potential demand for different shaving products. they agreed that it would be helpful to gather data on market size, cagr (compound annual growth rate), and pricing trends. rohan suggested prioritizing product categories based on market potential, rather than launching a full range of products. seema samanta offered to research market data and provide insights on which product categories to prioritize. rohan emphasized the importance of focusing on categories with proven demand, rather than investing in niche products. they discussed the need to assess the competitive landscape and identify opportunities to differentiate their products.", "growth stand-up & task delegation: brief mention of the growth stand-up as a potential time for discussion. harsh offered to take over the social media dashboard task if it wasn't completed. this was a consequence of the ongoing conflict regarding ownership and accountability.", "task completion & deadline - growth stand-up: harsh sharma emphasizes the need for a thorough approach to the task, stating there are no shortcuts. he acknowledges the recipient has been given sufficient time to complete the work (three weeks). harsh explicitly sets a deadline for completion: 'tonight's growth stand-up'. harsh offers to discuss any issues or roadblocks the recipient may be facing, encouraging them to message him. harsh states he will connect with the recipient in the evening to follow up. the conversation suggests a previous discussion about the task's timeline and acceptable quality. there's an implicit expectation that the task is nearing completion and should be ready for review during the stand-up. the tone is firm but offers support, indicating a desire for completion while remaining approachable. the use of 'quick and dirty' implies a previous suggestion to take a faster, potentially less thorough approach, which was rejected. the exchange is brief and focused solely on task completion and a follow-up plan. harsh reiterates the importance of thoroughness, contrasting it with a faster, less detailed method. the closing remarks ('okay. okay. bye. bye. bye.') are perfunctory and signal the end of the discussion.", "introduction of harsh & project overview: ayush introduces harsh sharma as the new generalist growth team member. harsh will work on projects related